<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RUT_GenStep_DeepBlackMere.xml   RM_TheSump — SUMP_TAR_HYDROLOGY_1 ruling 7

  GenStepDef for RUT_GenStep_DeepBlackMere.cs (this same pass). A GenStepDef
  on its own runs on no map; registration is the separate
  Patches/RUT_GenStep_DeepBlackMere_Register.xml (same split
  RUT_SumpTarBeastGenStep.xml/_Register.xml already use, read directly
  before writing this).

  order 225: after vanilla terrain generation (210/220, this mod's own
  precedent) and well ahead of RUT_GenStep_TarBeastPlacement (780) — the
  mere's own deep-tar cells should already exist on the map before that
  step's ScattererValidator_TerrainDef(RM_TarDeep) goes looking for a place
  to seat a dormant beast, so the mere itself becomes an eligible site for
  it. INVENTED-BUILD, same as that step's own order comment: no other
  Base_Player genStep order is named by anything this pass read.

  No MayRequire on the def itself: the class self-gates on the map's biome
  and a soft terrain lookup (RM_TarDeep may be absent), so this is always
  safe to declare. The Register patch below gates the class REFERENCE itself
  on mandrake.rm.thesump, matching every sibling registration in this file.
-->
<Defs>

  <GenStepDef>
    <defName>RUT_GenStep_DeepBlackMere</defName>
    <order>225</order>
    <genStep Class="RimMandrake.TheSump.RUT_GenStep_DeepBlackMere" />
  </GenStepDef>

</Defs>
